wsl-dns-forward
================

A DNS forwarder for the loopback address that makes .local (mDNS, Rendezvous,
Bonjour) host names resolve inside WSL2 on Windows 10, where WSL cannot see
the multicast traffic mDNS needs.  .local questions are answered through a
PowerShell helper running in Windows; everything else goes to the normal
upstream DNS server.

Read README.md for the problem, installation, setup and troubleshooting, and
wsl-dns-forward(8) for every option, fallback and diagnostic message.

Build:    ./configure --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc --localstatedir=/var
          make && make check && sudo make install
License:  ISC (see COPYING)
Source:   https://github.com/moebiusV/wsl-dns-forward
